# A NEW generated artifact does not need a line here: the wrappers in ./bin pass the
# repo's own .gitignore files as additional --ignore-path entries (prettier 3.6
# accepts the flag repeatedly), so "gitignored => never formatted" holds by
# construction. That matters since #394: in write mode a generated file was
# silently rewritten on every push, in check mode it would BLOCK every push —
# a generated file must be able to do neither, and enumerating them reactively
# only re-arms the same failure the next time a tool writes somewhere new.
#
# The entries ABOVE stay: they are the floor for non-git contexts, where
# `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` fails and the delegation silently no-ops. Do not
# delete them expecting the delegation to cover them.

# Shipped workflow artifacts (#219) — a BYTE-IDENTICAL mirror of `.claude/workflows/`,
# which lives outside every package and is therefore formatted by nothing. Formatting only
# this copy would break the mirror guard that makes the two one artifact. Same reason the
# eslint config and the knowledge-hub vitest config exclude it: shipping a directory into a
# package brought it under three tool scopes it was never under, and all three must agree.
#
# `**/` is load-bearing. This file's patterns resolve against THIS directory (git semantics,
# see _ignore-args.sh), so a bare `dataset/.workflows/` would mean
# `tools/prettier-config/dataset/.workflows/` — a path that does not exist, silently
# matching nothing.
